From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DeviceManagerUiLib: hide the USB NIC's config formsets

CreateDeviceManagerForm() lists every platform-setup formset: NIC config
formsets (IP4/IP6/VLAN/HTTP-Boot) group under "Network Device List", keyed
by a MAC node in the owning handle's device path. The BMC's USB CDC
network gadget - the Redfish host interface - qualifies like any NIC, so
Setup offers IP and VLAN configuration for a fixed point-to-point
management link whose addressing comes from the SMBIOS type 42 record. An
edit there breaks Redfish discovery, and just browsing the forms pokes
the gadget's network stack, which patch 0102 exists to keep quiet.

Skip formsets whose owning handle's device path carries both a USB node
and a MAC node - the same test 0103 uses to keep USB NICs out of
boot-option enumeration. The skip must be total, not a failed network
test: a formset that fails IsNeedAddNetworkMenu() falls through to the
top level of Device Manager, which would surface the gadget's forms in a
worse place. Platform NICs (RP1 GEM) have no USB node and keep their
Network Device List entry; USB mass storage has no MAC node and keeps its
top-level entries.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform policy]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Library/DeviceManagerUiLib/DeviceManager.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Library/DeviceManagerUiLib/DeviceManager.c
@@ -344,6 +344,64 @@
 }
 
 /**
+  Check whether the formsets on an HII handle belong to a NIC carried over
+  USB.
+
+  A USB NIC's device path contains both a USB node and a MAC node; platform
+  NICs (RP1 GEM) have no USB node and other USB devices publish no MAC node.
+  On this platform the only USB NIC is the BMC's CDC network gadget - the
+  Redfish host interface, a fixed point-to-point management link configured
+  from the SMBIOS type 42 record. Its IPv4/IPv6/VLAN/HTTP-Boot formsets must
+  stay out of Setup: an edit there would break Redfish discovery, and
+  browsing the forms pokes the gadget's network stack (the same policy that
+  keeps USB NICs out of BDS boot-option enumeration).
+
+  @param Handle  The HII handle to check.
+
+  @retval TRUE   The handle's formsets belong to a NIC carried over USB.
+  @retval FALSE  They do not (or the handle has no device path).
+
+**/
+STATIC
+BOOLEAN
+DmIsUsbNicHiiHandle (
+  IN EFI_HII_HANDLE  Handle
+  )
+{
+  EFI_STATUS                Status;
+  EFI_HANDLE                DriverHandle;
+  EFI_DEVICE_PATH_PROTOCOL  *Node;
+  BOOLEAN                   HasMac;
+  BOOLEAN                   OverUsb;
+
+  Status = gHiiDatabase->GetPackageListHandle (gHiiDatabase, Handle, &DriverHandle);
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    return FALSE;
+  }
+
+  Status = gBS->HandleProtocol (DriverHandle, &gEfiDevicePathProtocolGuid, (VOID **)&Node);
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    return FALSE;
+  }
+
+  HasMac  = FALSE;
+  OverUsb = FALSE;
+  for ( ; !IsDevicePathEnd (Node); Node = NextDevicePathNode (Node)) {
+    if (DevicePathType (Node) != MESSAGING_DEVICE_PATH) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    if (DevicePathSubType (Node) == MSG_USB_DP) {
+      OverUsb = TRUE;
+    } else if (DevicePathSubType (Node) == MSG_MAC_ADDR_DP) {
+      HasMac = TRUE;
+    }
+  }
+
+  return (BOOLEAN)(HasMac && OverUsb);
+}
+
+/**
   Check to see if the device path is for the network device.
 
   @param Handle          The HII handle which include the mac address device path.
@@ -623,6 +681,17 @@
           continue;
         }
 
+        //
+        // A NIC carried over USB is the BMC's CDC network gadget - the
+        // Redfish host interface. Skip its config formsets outright: they
+        // must neither join the Network Device List nor land on the top
+        // level, which is where a formset that merely failed
+        // IsNeedAddNetworkMenu() would fall through to below.
+        //
+        if (DmIsUsbNicHiiHandle (HiiHandles[Index])) {
+          break;
+        }
+
         String = HiiGetString (HiiHandles[Index], ((EFI_IFR_FORM_SET *)Ptr)->FormSetTitle, NULL);
         if (String == NULL) {
           String = HiiGetString (HiiHandle, STRING_TOKEN (STR_MISSING_STRING), NULL);
